.TH SMCTL 1 "2026-06-08" "smctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smctl \- control your Mac's System Management Controller from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smctl
.I subcommand
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smctl
is a CLI-first tool for controlling hardware that macOS normally manages on
its own \(em fan speed, battery charging, and power telemetry \(em on Apple
Silicon Macs.
.PP
Reading sensors works without privileges. Battery and fan control are applied
by a root LaunchDaemon,
.BR smctld ,
which the CLI talks to over XPC. Install it once with
.BR "sudo smctl daemon install" .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS sensors
.B smctl sensors
.RB [ --watch ]
.RB [ --json ]
.RS
Print temperatures (grouped by sensor), fan RPM and mode, battery, and package
power.
.B --watch
refreshes every second until interrupted;
.B --json
emits machine-readable output. Needs no daemon and no root.
.RE
.SS battery
.B smctl battery status
.RS
Charge level, charging state, and the configured limit.
.RE
.B smctl battery maintain
.IR LIMIT
.RS
Keep the charge within a limit. LIMIT is a single percent
.RI ( 80 ),
a range
.RI ( 70-80 ),
or
.B stop
to disable limiting. A dead-band prevents charge/discharge flapping near the
threshold.
.RE
.B smctl battery charge
.IR PERCENT
.RS
One-shot charge up to PERCENT, then stop.
.RE
.B smctl battery discharge
.IR PERCENT
.RS
Cut adapter power and discharge down to PERCENT. Runs in the foreground;
adapter power is restored on completion or interrupt.
.RE
.SS fan
.B smctl fan status
.RS
Per-fan actual, target, minimum, and maximum RPM, plus the control mode.
.RE
.B smctl fan set
.IR RPM
.RB [ --fan
.IR N ]
.RB [ --force ]
.RS
Set a manual fan target in RPM, clamped to the fan's reported min/max.
.B --fan
targets one fan (0-based); omit it to set all fans.
.B --force
permits targets below the minimum, but only when
.B allow_below_minimum
is set under
.B [safety]
in the config; the maximum is always a hard ceiling.
.RE
.B smctl fan auto
.RB [ --fan
.IR N ]
.RS
Return fans to system control.
.RE
.B smctl fan profile
.IR NAME
.RS
Apply a fan profile:
.BR auto ,
.BR quiet ,
.BR full ,
or a custom curve defined in the config.
.RE
.SS daemon
.B smctl daemon
.RB ( install | uninstall | restart | status | ping )
.RS
Manage
.BR smctld .
.B install/uninstall/restart
require root.
.B uninstall
restores system control of fans and charging before removing the daemon.
.B restart
reloads an upgraded binary \(em run it after every
.BR "brew upgrade" .
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Policy lives in
.IR /etc/smctl/config.toml ,
with sections
.BR [battery] ,
.BR [fan] ,
.BR [safety] ,
and
.BR [update] .
The daemon owns the file; CLI commands rewrite it. After hand-editing, run
.BR "sudo smctl daemon restart" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/smctl/config.toml
Declarative policy configuration.
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/one.leaper.smctl.daemon.plist
The installed LaunchDaemon.
.SH PRIVACY
The daemon makes one outbound request: a daily check of the GitHub releases API
for the latest version, surfaced by the CLI as an upgrade hint. Disable it with
.B check = false
under
.BR [update] .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B smctl
exits 0 on success and non-zero on error (64 for usage and validation errors).
.SH SEE ALSO
Project home and full documentation: https://github.com/leaperone/smctl
